text:
Since my mother passed XX/XX/XXXX, I have been in communication with the bank and their attorney. I was first told I needed to be identified ( registered ) as heir through heirship affidavit by a state agency. The bank attorney agreed and told me to call bank to verify. The bank agreed placed the account in forbearance, when I called back to say I was working to obtain that. The bank said that was not what I needed. They would not communicate with me for approximately 6 -9 months, until they filed to foreclose again. I got the heirship affidavit and that was exactly what was needed to be the confirmed the Successor In Interest. Since then to now, I have had to turn in documents and resubmit documents they have received and I call every other day for them to reach a decision while they are telling me to try to find other resources through the state ( TX ) while they send me emails repeatedly on the same days of a video of out of state I can not apply for and more recently a Texas resource I have called numerous times and been told will not help me due to the bank not making a decision as it is my mother 's debt not my own. XXXX XXXX amount owed was {$9300.00} XXXX XXXX amount owed is {$37000.00}. 
First they rejected my application due to me not being my mother even having the death certificate on file, then they said I didn't require an application due to it being an FHA loan, only to later say since I turned in an application as I was requested they needed a tax form, only sign the middle of the form and check a box, which they rejected the day after I called in to confirm they received it as not having my SSN on it. Last week they said I needed to resend 3 pay stubs. One of which they had as 3 of my last pay stubs submitted. I have been fully transparent with the bank for what my earnings in and have shown more income than my mother earned at purchase. 
The original purchase was less than the full accelerated amount due {$180000.00}
